  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responding to the Ebola Epidemic: Emergency &amp; Early Recovery - 2nd EA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to further assist in the response to the Ebola emergency in Sierra Leone.
The recent Sierra Leone Ebola KAP (knowledge, attitude and practice) Survey Report indicates that: &#x201C;awareness of Ebola is high, denial is low, but there are serious misconceptions, and comprehensive knowledge on EVD is low, and very high stigma and discrimination toward EVD victims persists.&#x201D;  The survey concludes that more work is needed on the social mobilization pillar, as there are still many people who continue to touch the dead bodies of their relatives, or look after sick people, or hide them at home.  

The project is aimed to establish and support village Ebola teams (VETs) to monitor and reinforce behavioural change from house to house within village communities in the Freetown Rural settlements in the Dioceses of Freetown, as it remains one of the hot sport districts with new infection EVD cases in Sierra Leone.</narrative>
  </description>
